    "title": "Verifiable Homeostatic Manifold Discovery in Quantum Oscillator Networks",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19984418",
    "publication_date": "2026-05-02",
    "description": "<p>We present a production-ready framework for verifiable self-organization in networks of 768 coupled quantum oscillators (the &ldquo;Crystal Brain&rdquo;), integrating six<br>fine-tuned components: adaptive SPSA optimization with automatic plateau escape, multi-resolution Louvain community detection, non-deterministic proof seeds,<br>normalized causal efficacy metrics, dynamic Merkle root hashing, and a semantic<br>proof-tagging API. We map the Ising regime classification of Bhalla et al. (2026)<br>onto a Kuramoto-type phase dynamics and demonstrate convergence to a coherent<br>CAPTURE regime with 84.7% capture fraction. A companion octonionic atlas of 50<br>nuclides (OctoSpec v0.4) reveals a moderate anti-correlation (r = &minus;0.54, p &lt; 0.001)<br>between the Octonionic Anomaly Index and nuclear binding energy. All coherence<br>milestones are certified by zero-knowledge proofs generated at 80-bit security via<br>the ZEE200 backend and registered immutably on the ARKHE OCTRA chain.</p>",
